<p>AMR = Agricultural Market Rate.</p>
<p>RMG = Real Monetary Gap.</p>
<p>On the basis of exchange rates on 11-13 December, the average RMG for the Irish punt is above +5 percent at 6.975 percent. The Irish green rate is therefore forecast to enter its fourth confirmation period on December 21 prior to a possible revaluation on January 11.</p>
<p>Since the average RMG for sterling is also greater than +5 percent at 6.374 percent it is currently forecast to enter its second of a possible five confirmation periods on December 21, prior to a potential revaluation on January 21.</p>
<p>All other green rates are currently forecast to remain unchanged from December 21.</p>
<p>During confirmation periods the three-day (six percent) rule is suspended.</p>
